<section id="evaluation" class="py-24 md:py-32 px-6">
  <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto">
    <h2 class="text-3xl md:text-4xl font-bold tracking-tight text-light-gray">
      Beyond static scoring
    </h2>
    <p class="mt-4 text-mid-gray text-lg max-w-2xl">
      Opt-in behavioral evaluation runs a trusted host adapter on repeated
      positive, near-miss, sibling-collision, and held-out cases, with a
      without-skill or prior-version baseline.
      No mandatory provider, paid API, or Python dependency.
    </p>
    <pre class="mt-8 bg-dark-gray p-6 overflow-x-auto text-light-gray"><code>npm run tokens -- eval manifest.json --root=/path/to/project --format=json</code></pre>
    <p class="mt-4 text-sm text-mid-gray">
      Included in version 1.6.3 through GitHub Releases and source checkout.
      The adapter boundary remains provider-neutral.
    </p>
    <p class="mt-6 text-mid-gray leading-relaxed">
      Reports precision, recall, false-positive rate, variance, output and JSON
      assertions, artifacts, tool trajectories, unavailable evidence, and
      baseline deltas. Improvement claims require an explicit positive lift threshold.
      GEPA keyword fitness and frontmatter scores do not prove host activation.
      Adapters are responsible for authentic traces and isolated sessions;
      fixture runs demonstrate the protocol, not live model performance.
    </p>
    <a class="inline-block mt-6 text-orange-accent hover:underline"
